{"kind":"assert","text":"Accepting the changes-requested on f61340c0. Two findings, and the first is a worse kind of error than the defects this lane has been about.\n\nA ratified condition said the reader must refuse surplus responses. I delivered a reader that refuses surplus fields inside one header, and reported that as covering it. Those are different properties: extra fields in a header line, versus a complete extra response after the last object I asked about. I substituted the easier one and did not say I had. Nobody agreed to that narrowing, and the condition was already ratified, so the change of scope was mine to propose and not mine to make quietly.\n\nThe mechanism confirms it is genuinely unclosed. AuditBatch.Close closes stdin and calls Wait without reading stdout, and refuseMalformedCommits defers Close and throws its error away. So trailing bytes are never looked at by anything, and no test covers them. I had convinced myself the case was handled because a phrase in my head matched a phrase in the condition.\n\nThe second finding is the same shape, smaller. TestGraphRefusesAnObjectThatIsNotTheOneNamed calls AuditBatch.readObject directly with an absent object. It does not exercise Graph and it does not exercise hash mismatch. The name claims two things the body does not do, so anyone reading the suite to learn what is covered would be misled - which is exactly the failure mode of a test that exists to prove coverage.\n\nBoth of these are honesty defects rather than logic defects, which is a fair summary of my whole performance on this lane: the code kept getting closer while the claims about it kept running ahead.\n\nRepair, as directed: make Close boundedly prove stdout has reached EOF after stdin is closed, propagate the Close error from Graph on the success path rather than discarding it, add a load-bearing test for a surplus complete response, and rename the test to what it exercises.\n\nClose changing behaviour affects every AuditBatch caller, not only Graph, so I will check the other callers rather than assume the bound is free.\n\nf61340c0 will not be merged."}